{"id":"mahabharata-12-276","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":276,"title":"षट्सप्तत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 276 · What is the highest good","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira, doubting the scriptures, asks what is the highest good for a man who has not resolved on a course. Bhishma tells him the teaching of Narada, that giving up egotism and checking attachment, with contentment and solitary conduct, is the unshaken good.","kn":"ಶಾಸ್ತ್ರಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಸಂಶಯ ಹೊಂದಿದ, ದಾರಿ ನಿಶ್ಚಯಿಸದ ಮನುಷ್ಯನಿಗೆ ಪರಮ ಶ್ರೇಯಸ್ಸು ಯಾವುದೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅಹಂಕಾರ ತ್ಯಾಗ, ಆಸಕ್ತಿ ನಿಗ್ರಹ, ಸಂತೋಷ, ಏಕಾಂತ ನಡೆಯೇ ಅಚಲ ಶ್ರೇಯಸ್ಸೆಂದು ನಾರದನ ಉಪದೇಶವನ್ನು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"शास्त्रों पर संशय करते और मार्ग तय न कर पाने वाले मनुष्य के लिए परम श्रेय क्या है, यह युधिष्ठिर पूछते हैं। भीष्म नारद का उपदेश सुनाते हैं कि अहंकार का त्याग, आसक्ति का निग्रह, सन्तोष और एकान्त आचरण ही अचल श्रेय है।","te":"శాస్త్రాలపై సందేహపడే, మార్గం నిర్ణయించుకోని మనిషికి పరమ శ్రేయస్సు ఏదని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు. అహంకార త్యాగం, ఆసక్తి నిగ్రహం, సంతోషం, ఏకాంత ప్రవర్తనే అచల శ్రేయస్సని నారదుని బోధను భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు.","ta":"நூல்களில் ஐயம் கொண்டு வழியை முடிவு செய்யாத மனிதனுக்கு உயர்ந்த நன்மை எது என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, அகங்காரத்தைத் துறத்தல், பற்றை அடக்குதல், மனநிறைவு, தனிமை ஒழுக்கம் ஆகியவையே அசையாத நன்மை என்று நாரதரின் போதனையைப் பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார்.","ml":"ശാസ്ത്രങ്ങളെ സംശയിച്ച യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ, ഒരു വഴി തീരുമാനിക്കാത്ത മനുഷ്യന് ഉത്തമമായ നന്മയേതെന്ന് ചോദിക്കുന്നു. അഹംഭാവം ഉപേക്ഷിച്ച്, ആസക്തി നിയന്ത്രിച്ച്, സംതൃപ്തിയോടെയും ഏകാന്തമായ നടപ്പോടെയും ജീവിക്കുന്നതാണ് ഇളകാത്ത നന്മയെന്ന് നാരദന്റെ ഉപദേശം ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.276; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अतत्त्वज्ञस्य शास्त्राणां सततं संशयात्मनः ।\nअकृतव्यवसायस्य श्रेयो ब्रूहि पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Grandfather, tell me the highest good for one who does not know the truth of the scriptures, who is ever in doubt and has made no firm resolve."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"गुरुपूजा च सततं वृद्धानां पर्युपासनम् ।\nश्रवणं चैव विद्यानां कूटस्थं श्रेय उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Constant service to the teacher, attending on the elders, and listening to the sciences are said to be the unchanging highest good."}},{"n":3,"text":"अत्राप्युदाहरन्तीममितिहासं पुरातनम् ।\nगालवस्य च संवादं देवर्षेर्नारदस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this subject too they cite an ancient account, the conversation of Galava and the divine sage Narada."}},{"n":4,"text":"वीतमोहक्लमं विप्रं ज्ञानतृप्तं जितेन्द्रियम् ।\nश्रेयस्कामं जितात्मानं नारदं गालवोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Galava spoke to Narada, a Brahmin free of delusion and weariness, content with knowledge, master of his senses and self, who desired the highest good:"}},{"n":5,"text":"यैः कैश्चित्संमतो लोके गुणैस्तु पुरुषो नृषु ।\nभवत्यनपगान्सर्वांस्तान्गुणाँल्लक्षयाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever qualities make a man esteemed among people in the world, I see all of those qualities undiminished in you."}},{"n":6,"text":"भवानेवंविधोऽस्माकं संशयं छेत्तुमर्हति ।\nअमूढश्चिरमूढानां लोकतत्त्वमजानताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man like you, undeluded, can cut the doubt of us who have long been deluded and do not know the truth of the world."}},{"n":7,"text":"ज्ञाने ह्येवं प्रवृत्तिः स्यात्कार्याकार्ये विजानतः ।\nयत्कार्यं न व्यवस्यामस्तद्भवान्वक्तुमर्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"For when one knows what should and should not be done, action follows from knowledge. Tell us what we cannot decide ought to be done."}},{"n":8,"text":"भगवन्नाश्रमाः सर्वे पृथगाचारदर्शिनः ।\nइदं श्रेय इदं श्रेय इति नानाप्रधाविताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sir, all the orders of life see different practices, and people rush about in many directions saying, \"This is the highest good, this is.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"तांस्तु विप्रस्थितान्दृष्ट्वा शास्त्रैः शास्त्राभिनन्दिनः ।\nस्वशास्त्रैः परितुष्टांश्च श्रेयो नोपलभामहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them divided by their scriptures, each delighted in his own scripture and content with it, we cannot find the highest good."}},{"n":10,"text":"शास्त्रं यदि भवेदेकं व्यक्तं श्रेयो भवेत्तदा ।\nशास्त्रैश्च बहुभिर्भूयः श्रेयो गुह्यं प्रवेशितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If there were only one scripture, the highest good would be plain; but with many scriptures the highest good has been made a hidden thing."}},{"n":11,"text":"एतस्मात्कारणाच्छ्रेयः कलिलं प्रतिभाति माम् ।\nब्रवीतु भगवांस्तन्मे उपसन्नोऽस्म्यधीहि भोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For this reason the highest good seems clouded to me. Tell it to me, sir; I have come to you as a pupil, so teach me."}},{"text":"नारद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Narada said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"आश्रमास्तात चत्वारो यथासंकल्पिताः पृथक् ।\nतान्सर्वाननुपश्य त्वं समाश्रित्यैव गालव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear Galava, the four orders of life are laid out separately as intended; take refuge in each and look at all of them."}},{"n":13,"text":"तेषां तेषां तथा हि त्वमाश्रमाणां ततस्ततः ।\nनानारूपगुणोद्देशं पश्य विप्रस्थितं पृथक् ।\nनयन्ति चैव ते सम्यगभिप्रेतमसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise look separately at the varied qualities and aims set out in each of those orders. They lead one rightly and without doubt to the intended end."}},{"n":14,"text":"ऋजु पश्यंस्तथा सम्यगाश्रमाणां परां गतिम् ।\nयत्तु निःश्रेयसं सम्यक्तच्चैवासंशयात्मकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing straight, you will see the supreme goal of the orders of life; and what is the true highest good is free from doubt."}},{"n":15,"text":"अनुग्रहं च मित्राणाममित्राणां च निग्रहम् ।\nसंग्रहं च त्रिवर्गस्य श्रेय आहुर्मनीषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise call the highest good kindness to friends, restraint of enemies, and keeping up the three aims of life."}},{"n":16,"text":"निवृत्तिः कर्मणः पापात्सततं पुण्यशीलता ।\nसद्भिश्च समुदाचारः श्रेय एतदसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Turning away from sinful action, constant virtuous conduct, and good dealings with the good: this is without doubt the highest good."}},{"n":17,"text":"मार्दवं सर्वभूतेषु व्यवहारेषु चार्जवम् ।\nवाक्चैव मधुरा प्रोक्ता श्रेय एतदसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gentleness to all beings, honesty in dealings and kind speech: this is without doubt the highest good."}},{"n":18,"text":"देवताभ्यः पितृभ्यश्च संविभागोऽतिथिष्वपि ।\nअसंत्यागश्च भृत्यानां श्रेय एतदसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sharing with the gods, the ancestors and guests, and not abandoning one's dependents: this is without doubt the highest good."}},{"n":19,"text":"सत्यस्य वचनं श्रेयः सत्यज्ञानं तु दुष्करम् ।\nयद्भूतहितमत्यन्तमेतत्सत्यं ब्रवीम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Speaking truth is the highest good, but knowing truth is hard; what is utterly beneficial to beings, that I call truth."}},{"n":20,"text":"अहंकारस्य च त्यागः प्रणयस्य च निग्रहः ।\nसंतोषश्चैकचर्या च कूटस्थं श्रेय उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Giving up egoism, curbing attachment, contentment and a solitary life are said to be the unchanging highest good."}},{"n":21,"text":"धर्मेण वेदाध्ययनं वेदाङ्गानां तथैव च ।\nविद्यार्थानां च जिज्ञासा श्रेय एतदसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Studying the Veda according to dharma, and the Vedangas too, and seeking the meaning of the sciences: this is without doubt the highest good."}},{"n":22,"text":"शब्दरूपरसस्पर्शान्सह गन्धेन केवलान् ।\nनात्यर्थमुपसेवेत श्रेयसोऽर्थी परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who seeks the highest good, scorcher of foes, should not indulge excessively in sound, form, taste, touch and smell taken alone."}},{"n":23,"text":"नक्तंचर्या दिवास्वप्नमालस्यं पैशुनं मदम् ।\nअतियोगमयोगं च श्रेयसोऽर्थी परित्यजेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who seeks the highest good should give up prowling at night, sleeping by day, laziness, slander, pride, excess and neglect."}},{"n":24,"text":"कर्मोत्कर्षं न मार्गेत परेषां परिनिन्दया ।\nस्वगुणैरेव मार्गेत विप्रकर्षं पृथग्जनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He should not seek distinction in action by disparaging others; he should seek to rise above the common man by his own virtues."}},{"n":25,"text":"निर्गुणास्त्वेव भूयिष्ठमात्मसंभाविनो नराः ।\nदोषैरन्यान्गुणवतः क्षिपन्त्यात्मगुणक्षयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men without virtue, mostly full of self-regard, run down the virtuous by pointing out faults, so as to make their own failings less."}},{"n":26,"text":"अनुच्यमानाश्च पुनस्ते मन्यन्ते महाजनात् ।\nगुणवत्तरमात्मानं स्वेन मानेन दर्पिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And though no one speaks of them, they think themselves, swollen with their own estimate, more virtuous than the great."}},{"n":27,"text":"अब्रुवन्कस्यचिन्निन्दामात्मपूजामवर्णयन् ।\nविपश्चिद्गुणसंपन्नः प्राप्नोत्येव महद्यशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise man rich in virtue, without speaking ill of anyone or describing his own praise, wins great fame."}},{"n":28,"text":"अब्रुवन्वाति सुरभिर्गन्धः सुमनसां शुचिः ।\nतथैवाव्याहरन्भाति विमलो भानुरम्बरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The pure fragrance of flowers spreads without speaking, and the spotless sun shines in the sky without a word."}},{"n":29,"text":"एवमादीनि चान्यानि परित्यक्तानि मेधया ।\nज्वलन्ति यशसा लोके यानि न व्याहरन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"These and other things the wise give up; yet in the world they blaze with fame without announcing themselves."}},{"n":30,"text":"न लोके दीप्यते मूर्खः केवलात्मप्रशंसया ।\nअपि चापिहितः श्वभ्रे कृतविद्यः प्रकाशते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A fool does not shine in the world by self-praise alone; but the learned man shines though hidden in a pit."}},{"n":31,"text":"असन्नुच्चैरपि प्रोक्तः शब्दः समुपशाम्यति ।\nदीप्यते त्वेव लोकेषु शनैरपि सुभाषितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A false statement, even loudly proclaimed, dies away; but a good saying, even softly spoken, gradually shines in the world."}},{"n":32,"text":"मूढानामवलिप्तानामसारं भाषितं बहु ।\nदर्शयत्यन्तरात्मानं दिवा रूपमिवांशुमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The much empty talk of the deluded and the proud displays their inner self, as the sun by day reveals form."}},{"n":33,"text":"एतस्मात्कारणात्प्रज्ञां मृगयन्ते पृथग्विधाम् ।\nप्रज्ञालाभो हि भूतानामुत्तमः प्रतिभाति माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For this reason people seek wisdom of various kinds; to me the gaining of wisdom seems the best thing for beings."}},{"n":34,"text":"नापृष्टः कस्यचिद्ब्रूयान्न चान्यायेन पृच्छतः ।\nज्ञानवानपि मेधावी जडवल्लोकमाचरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should not speak to anyone unasked, nor to one who asks improperly; even a learned and clever man should act in the world like a dullard."}},{"n":35,"text":"ततो वासं परीक्षेत धर्मनित्येषु साधुषु ।\nमनुष्येषु वदान्येषु स्वधर्मनिरतेषु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he should examine a place to live, among good people constant in dharma, generous men devoted to their own duty."}},{"n":36,"text":"चतुर्णां यत्र वर्णानां धर्मव्यतिकरो भवेत् ।\nन तत्र वासं कुर्वीत श्रेयोर्थी वै कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where the duties of the four classes are mixed up, one who seeks the highest good should in no way make his home."}},{"n":37,"text":"निरारम्भोऽप्ययमिह यथालब्धोपजीवनः ।\nपुण्यं पुण्येषु विमलं पापं पापेषु चाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even without undertaking work, one who lives here on what comes his way gains spotless merit among the meritorious and sin among the sinful."}},{"n":38,"text":"अपामग्नेस्तथेन्दोश्च स्पर्शं वेदयते यथा ।\nतथा पश्यामहे स्पर्शमुभयोः पापपुण्ययोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As one feels the touch of water, fire and the moon, so we see the touch of both sin and merit."}},{"n":39,"text":"अपश्यन्तोऽन्नविषयं भुञ्जते विघसाशिनः ।\nभुञ्जानं चान्नविषयान्विषयं विद्धि कर्मणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who eat leftovers eat food without seeing its source; but know that the one who eats food is the very object of his deeds."}},{"n":40,"text":"यत्रागमयमानानामसत्कारेण पृच्छताम् ।\nप्रब्रूयाद्ब्रह्मणो धर्मं त्यजेत्तं देशमात्मवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where a man of the Brahmin class who is unprepared and asks without respect would be taught dharma, the self-possessed man should leave that region."}},{"n":41,"text":"शिष्योपाध्यायिका वृत्तिर्यत्र स्यात्सुसमाहिता ।\nयथावच्छास्त्रसंपन्ना कस्तं देशं परित्यजेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where the livelihood of pupil and teacher is well kept and fully equipped with scripture, who would leave that region?"}},{"n":42,"text":"आकाशस्था ध्रुवं यत्र दोषं ब्रूयुर्विपश्चिताम् ।\nआत्मपूजाभिकामा वै को वसेत्तत्र पण्डितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where those standing aloof surely speak ill of the learned, desiring their own worship, what wise man would live there?"}},{"n":43,"text":"यत्र संलोडिता लुब्धैः प्रायशो धर्मसेतवः ।\nप्रदीप्तमिव शैलान्तं कस्तं देशं न संत्यजेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where the bridges of dharma have mostly been broken up by the greedy, who would not leave that region, as one leaves the edge of a mountain on fire?"}},{"n":44,"text":"यत्र धर्ममनाशङ्काश्चरेयुर्वीतमत्सराः ।\nचरेत्तत्र वसेच्चैव पुण्यशीलेषु साधुषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where people practice dharma without fear and free of envy, one should go about and live among those good people of virtuous conduct."}},{"n":45,"text":"धर्ममर्थनिमित्तं तु चरेयुर्यत्र मानवाः ।\nन ताननुवसेज्जातु ते हि पापकृतो जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where people practice dharma for the sake of gain, one should never live among them, for they are doers of sin."}},{"n":46,"text":"कर्मणा यत्र पापेन वर्तन्ते जीवितेस्पवः ।\nव्यवधावेत्ततस्तूर्णं ससर्पाच्छरणादिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where people live by sinful action, desiring to live, one should run quickly away from there, as from a house with a snake."}},{"n":47,"text":"येन खट्वां समारूढः कर्मणानुशयी भवेत् ।\nआदितस्तन्न कर्तव्यमिच्छता भवमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By whatever action one lies on a bed repenting afterward, that should not be done from the start by one who wishes his own well-being."}},{"n":48,"text":"यत्र राजा च राज्ञश्च पुरुषाः प्रत्यनन्तराः ।\nकुटुम्बिनामग्रभुजस्त्यजेत्तद्राष्ट्रमात्मवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where the king and the king's men next in rank eat before the householders, the self-possessed man should leave that kingdom."}},{"n":49,"text":"श्रोत्रियास्त्वग्रभोक्तारो धर्मनित्याः सनातनाः ।\nयाजनाध्यापने युक्ता यत्र तद्राष्ट्रमावसेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Live in the kingdom where learned Brahmins, constant in dharma and eternal, eat first and are engaged in sacrificing and teaching."}},{"n":50,"text":"स्वाहास्वधावषट्कारा यत्र सम्यगनुष्ठिताः ।\nअजस्रं चैव वर्तन्ते वसेत्तत्राविचारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where the offerings of svaha, svadha and vashat are duly performed and go on without break, live there without hesitation."}},{"n":51,"text":"अशुचीन्यत्र पश्येत ब्राह्मणान्वृत्तिकर्शितान् ।\nत्यजेत्तद्राष्ट्रमासन्नमुपसृष्टमिवामिषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where one sees Brahmins unclean and wasted by want of livelihood, leave that kingdom at hand like meat that flies have settled on."}},{"n":52,"text":"प्रीयमाणा नरा यत्र प्रयच्छेयुरयाचिताः ।\nस्वस्थचित्तो वसेत्तत्र कृतकृत्य इवात्मवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where people give gladly without being asked, live there with a tranquil mind, like one who has done his duty."}},{"n":53,"text":"दण्डो यत्राविनीतेषु सत्कारश्च कृतात्मसु ।\nचरेत्तत्र वसेच्चैव पुण्यशीलेषु साधुषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where punishment falls on the unruly and honor on the self-controlled, go about and live there among good people of virtuous conduct."}},{"n":54,"text":"उपसृष्टेष्वदान्तेषु दुराचारेष्वसाधुषु ।\nअविनीतेषु लुब्धेषु सुमहद्दण्डधारणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where the afflicted, uncontrolled, ill-behaved, wicked, unruly and greedy are visited with very heavy punishment, live there."}},{"n":55,"text":"यत्र राजा धर्मनित्यो राज्यं वै पर्युपासिता ।\nअपास्य कामान्कामेशो वसेत्तत्राविचारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where the king is constant in dharma and serves the kingdom, giving up desires though master of them, live there without hesitation."}},{"n":56,"text":"तथाशीला हि राजानः सर्वान्विषयवासिनः ।\nश्रेयसा योजयन्त्याशु श्रेयसि प्रत्युपस्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kings of such character quickly bring all dwellers in the land to the highest good, when the highest good presents itself."}},{"n":57,"text":"पृच्छतस्ते मया तात श्रेय एतदुदाहृतम् ।\nन हि शक्यं प्रधानेन श्रेयः संख्यातुमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear Galava, you asked me and I have told you this highest good; for the highest good of the self cannot be counted out in its main points."}},{"n":58,"text":"एवं प्रवर्तमानस्य वृत्तिं प्रणिहितात्मनः ।\nतपसैवेह बहुलं श्रेयो व्यक्तं भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one who lives this way, with a steady mind, the highest good will become plain, through austerity alone, in abundance."}}]}]}